# Tiger Style (ReAct dialect)

Normative: `specs/tiger-style.md`, decision **R1**. Skill: **`tiger-style`**.

## Two layers

- **Kernel** (`react-core`): pure given injected world; consistent; **effectively exactly-once** under retry.
- **Host / adapters**: real I/O; MAY be at-least-once (network, LLM). Kernel EOS MUST NOT be sold as product EOS; host at-least-once MUST NOT weaken the kernel.

## Runtime

- Async, event-based, **multi-threaded** — OK and expected.
- MUST NOT require process-wide single-threading for correctness.
- Logical ownership via types + monotonics + OCC. Logical time is an injected **Clock**.

## Kernel durable paths

- Idempotency key (or natural key) + durable dedupe/result.
- Commit boundary: state + side effect together or neither.
- Conditional writes; conflict → abort/retry with a fresh read.
- Fixed safety ceilings (budgets, payload, in-flight) in code — not operator knobs.
- Assert / fail-closed on protocol, tenancy, budget — no silent fallbacks.
- **No external side effects** in the kernel (`std::env`, FS, net, wall clock, OS RNG).

## Auto-tune

- Pools, channels, memory targets, batches, depths derive from hardware/load under ceilings.
- MUST NOT grow env knobs for those. Product config (model, bind, storage URI) stays explicit.
- Buffers/channels stay bounded.

## Simulation

- Same owner code under a seeded simulator. MUST NOT `sleep` as correctness.
- Fuzz MAY mutate codecs/schedules; MUST NOT replace the checker.

## Anti-patterns

- Best-effort dual-write without dedupe.
- Unbounded buffers/channels.
- Last-write-wins on concurrent thread/store mutations without a decision.
- Impl env sprawl (`FOO_BATCH_SIZE`, `WORKER_THREADS`, …).
- Test-only fork of the run loop. Sleep-based tests.
